# Git for Windows checks text files out with CRLF by default, which made
# `npm run check` fail on the Windows runner: scripts/sync-readme-versions.mjs
# compares blocks built with LF against a CRLF working tree and reports every
# README as stale. .editorconfig already asks for LF, but editors honour it and
# Git does not.
* text=auto eol=lf
